MID_SE_Max_Hal_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_001: Hmm...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_002: Hmm...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_003: Gotta get closer so I can see... Wait—he's gone?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_004: Heh heh HEH! Gotcha! What do you want with the\nInfernal Clown, huh?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_005: Aah! How'd you do that?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_006: You answer me first! Somebody put you up to this?\nWere you trying to see my face?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_007: Tsk, tsk. Might have to teach you some manners.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_008: I wasn't trying to do anything weird! I just wanted to\nsee you perform...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_009: From one performer to another, I was impressed by\nhow committed you are to the role.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_010: Hmm... You better be telling the truth. What do you\nmean you're a "performer"?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_011: I used to be in Nasshim's Circus. I figured I could\nuse your tricks as reference or something.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_012: Aah! Nasshim's Circus?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_013: Oh, did you ever see us perform?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_014: Well... I know the name. And I know performing's\njust the half of what you do. Hehehe.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_015: Huh? What do you mean by that?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_016: I guess the truth's above your pay grade. Where's\nNasshim now?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_017: Well, he... I mean, we were attacked by bandits,\nand...I was the only one who made it.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_018: Oh, ha, I get it. So you never got a chance to learn\nthe truth.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_019: Word of advice—don't tell anyone you were in\nNasshim's Circus, OK?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_020: Hang on. You're acting funny... What makes you\nsay that?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_021: Heh heh HEH! I'm always acting funny! Gotta go—\nand you better not follow me this time.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_C_022: I wonder what he's getting at... Maybe he knows\nNasshim.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_001: Hey, um! Hang on!
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_002: You're in my way.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_003: Heh heh HEH. Aw, look at you shiver and shake!\nYou nervous?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_004: I mean...yeah, I'm nervous, but I still want to ask you\nabout something.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_005: It's about Nasshim... I want you to tell me what you\nknow about him.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_006: Ngh... Y'know, some things you're better off\nnot knowing.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_007: Maybe! But...he was really important to me.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_008: Alright, fine. I'll tell you what I know.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_009: I'd always heard Nasshim's troupe was a pack of\nbandits. Or—chivalrous thieves, to be generous.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_010: He was a bandit?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_011: Yeah. The guy had enemies everywhere. That's\nprobably why you were attacked.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_012: I see...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_013: Uh-huh. I see you aren't arguing with me.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_014: I don't want to believe it. But...it feels right.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_015: He did teach me how to fight... Maybe that was so\nI could steal things.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_016: Well, now you get why you shouldn't tell people\nyou were in Nasshim's Circus.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_017: You'll only be inviting bad blood. Oh, and stop using\nthe tricks he taught you.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_018: I can't do that! I don't want to give up on all of it...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_019: Even if Nasshim was hiding things from me...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_020: He was always kind to me, and he gave me a place\nto belong.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_021: So the things he taught me—they mean something to\nme. I'll do whatever it takes to keep performing.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_022: What, to honor his legacy? It's not like Nasshim\ncares. He's deadzo!
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_023: Ah! That's... But, I... *sob*
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_024: Tell you what. Maybe I can help you train.\nBuild on what you learned from him.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_025: You will? Thank you! But...why?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_026: Are you maybe actually a kind person?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_027: No, it's just... Training together gives me a good\nexcuse to slice you up!
MID_SE_Max_Hal_B_028: Eep... Even if you're scary, I've gotta do this.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_001: Maxim! I'm so glad you're safe.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_002: I'm relieved we both made it out.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_003: Me too. Honestly, without Jester's training, I\nmight've been a goner in that battle...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_004: No, I'm sure it had more to do with Nasshim's\nteachings.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_005: Hey, when you were Jester, you were also hiding\nfrom your pursuers, huh?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_006: And yet you told me what you knew about Nasshim\nand even took the time to train me...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_007: I don't know how I can thank you.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_008: You don't have to. I feel like I've done a little to pay\nback Nasshim for all the good he did.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_009: Standing up for the powerless—bringing more justice\nto the world.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_010: Oh yeah, you called our troupe "chivalrous thieves"\nat one point, didn't you?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_011: Mhm. He stole from crooks and the corrupt oligarchs\nto give to the people.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_012: I remember. After performances, Nasshim would\ninvite the villagers and have a feast.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_013: Normally, it would fall to the Aragonian knights to\npunish the thieves.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_014: But when corruption spread in the kingdom,\nwe couldn't even do that.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_015: By the time I left, we were hardly knights at all.\nMore like...assassins.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_016: I see...
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_017: That's how I learned about Nasshim. He'd been\ndocumented as a person of interest.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_018: I might've been powerless, but I could take solace\nknowing he was making a difference.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_019: So...I'm glad I could help protect you, the person he\nwas watching over.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_020: And you can go on living, giving people hope,\nand bringing joy to their lives.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_021: Thank you so much, Maxim. I'll continue to work on\nmy skills.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_022: In a world like this with war happening, I think it'd\nbe really nice to perform and make people smile.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_023: Yeah. Actually, on that note.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_024: Could I maybe come perform with you?
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_025: I'm not up to your level, but I do have some\nexperience from my Jester days.
MID_SE_Max_Hal_A_026: I'd love that, yeah! I'm sure if we perform together,\nwe'll get a standing ovation!